# Cursor Rules for Hugo Static Site Project

## Project Overview
This is a Hugo static site project using the Eureka theme, deployed to GitHub Pages.

## Technology Stack
- **Static Site Generator**: Hugo (v0.111.0, recommended v0.110.0+)
- **Theme**: Eureka v0.9.3 (wangchucheng.com/hugo-eureka)
- **Installation Method**: Hugo Modules (requires Go 1.12+)
- **Deployment**: GitHub Pages via GitHub Actions
- **Content Format**: Markdown with YAML frontmatter
- **Documentation**: 
  - Hugo: https://gohugo.io/documentation/
  - Eureka: https://www.wangchucheng.com/zh/docs/hugo-eureka/getting-started/

## Project Structure
- `content/` - All content files (posts, docs, pages, authors)
  - `content/posts/` - Blog posts/articles
  - `content/docs/` - Documentation pages (hierarchical structure)
  - `content/homepage/` - Homepage widgets and pages
  - `content/authors/` - Author information
- `config/_default/` - Hugo configuration files
  - `config.yaml` - Main configuration
  - `params.yaml` - Theme parameters and settings
  - `menus.yaml` - Navigation menu configuration
  - `languages.yaml` - Language settings
- `layouts/` - Custom templates and layouts (overrides theme templates)
  - `layouts/_default/` - Default page templates
  - `layouts/partials/` - Reusable template partials
  - `layouts/components/` - Template components
- `static/` - Static assets (images, JS, CSS) - copied directly to output
- `assets/` - Source assets that may be processed by Hugo Pipes
- `archetypes/` - Content templates for `hugo new` command
- `.github/workflows/` - GitHub Actions workflows
- `go.mod` - Hugo Modules configuration

## Content Management

### Content Types (Eureka Archetypes)
Eureka provides several content types via archetypes:
- **posts**: Blog posts/articles (`hugo new posts/article-name.md`)
- **docs**: Documentation pages (`hugo new docs/topic/doc-name.md`)
- **homepage**: Homepage widgets (`hugo new homepage/page-name.md`)
- **authors**: Author profiles (`hugo new -k authors authors/author-name`)

### Content File Structure
- All content files use Markdown format with YAML frontmatter
- Frontmatter must include: `title`, `date`, `draft` (set to `false` for published content)
- Optional frontmatter: `description`, `tags`, `categories`, `authors`, `series`, `featuredImage`, `toc`, `enableComment`
- Use `hugo new` command to create content with proper archetype templates

### Content Organization
- **Posts**: `content/posts/` - Flat structure, use tags and categories for organization
- **Docs**: `content/docs/` - Hierarchical structure (e.g., `docs/topic/details/doc.md`)
  - Use `_index.md` files for section landing pages
- **Homepage**: `content/homepage/` - Widget-based pages (experience, about, etc.)
- **Authors**: `content/authors/` - Author profiles with `_index.md` for author listing

### Draft Content
- Set `draft: true` in frontmatter to prevent publishing
- Use `hugo server -D` to preview draft content locally
- Drafts are excluded from production builds

## Code Style Guidelines
- Use consistent Markdown formatting
- Frontmatter should include: title, date, tags/categories when applicable
- Follow existing content structure patterns
- Use Chinese language for content (defaultContentLanguage: zh)
- Date format: ISO 8601 (e.g., `2025-01-15T16:10:00+08:00`)
- Use YAML frontmatter (not TOML or JSON)

## Hugo Commands

### Development
- `hugo server` - Start local development server (http://localhost:1313)
- `hugo server -D` - Include draft content in preview
- `hugo server --bind 0.0.0.0 --port 1313` - Bind to all interfaces

### Content Creation
- `hugo new posts/article-name.md` - Create new post
- `hugo new docs/topic/doc-name.md` - Create new documentation page
- `hugo new -k authors authors/author-name` - Create author profile
- `hugo new homepage/page-name.md` - Create homepage widget

### Building
- `hugo` - Build site (excludes drafts)
- `hugo --gc --minify` - Build for production with garbage collection and minification
- `hugo --cleanDestinationDir` - Clean destination directory before build

### Hugo Modules
- `hugo mod download` - Download Hugo Modules dependencies
- `hugo mod clean` - Clean module cache
- `hugo mod tidy` - Remove unused dependencies

## Configuration Files

### config.yaml (Main Configuration)
- `baseURL`: https://zjingwang.github.io/
- `theme`: wangchucheng.com/hugo-eureka (Hugo Modules)
- `defaultContentLanguage`: zh (Chinese)
- `hasCJKLanguage`: true (for Chinese/Japanese/Korean)
- `paginate`: 3 (posts per page) - Note: deprecated in v0.128.0+, use `pagination.pagerSize` instead
- `taxonomies`: categories, tags, series, authors
- `markup`: Goldmark renderer with table of contents support
- `outputs`: HTML, RSS, JSON for home page

### params.yaml (Eureka Theme Settings)
- `mainSections`: ["posts"] - Main content sections
- `siteType`: Person - Schema.org type
- `colorScheme`: auto/light/dark - Theme color mode
- `highlight`: Code highlighting (highlightjs)
- `math`: Math rendering (katex)
- `comment`: Comment system (utterances/disqus/valine/commento)
- `icon`: Site icon path
- `dateFormat`: Date display format

### menus.yaml (Navigation)
- Define main navigation menu items
- Each item has: `name`, `url`, `weight` (for ordering)
- Current menu: 关于我, 文章, 日常, 其他, 日志, 统计

### languages.yaml (Multilingual)
- Configure language-specific settings
- Default language: zh (Chinese)
- `defaultContentLanguageInSubdir`: true

## Hugo Core Concepts

### Content Organization
- Hugo uses a content-first approach
- Content files are organized by type and section
- Frontmatter defines metadata and behavior
- Markdown content follows frontmatter

### Templates and Layouts
- Templates use Go template syntax
- Layout hierarchy: `_default/baseof.html` → section layout → type layout
- Partials are reusable template fragments
- Lookup order: `layouts/` → `themes/eureka/layouts/`
- Custom layouts in `layouts/` override theme layouts
- Use `{{ partial "partial-name.html" . }}` to include partials

### Hugo Pipes
- Process assets (CSS, JS, images) during build
- Use `resources.Get` and `resources.FromString` in templates
- Supports PostCSS, SASS, minification, etc.
- Assets in `assets/` are processed, `static/` are copied as-is
- If encountering POSTCSS errors, ensure Hugo version is 0.100.0 or higher

### Taxonomies
- Default: categories, tags
- Custom: series, authors
- Access in templates via `.Site.Taxonomies`
- Taxonomy pages auto-generated
- Use `{{ range .Site.Taxonomies.tags }}` to iterate

### Shortcodes
- Reusable content snippets: `{{< shortcode-name >}}`
- Eureka provides built-in shortcodes
- Custom shortcodes in `layouts/shortcodes/`
- Use `{{< shortcode param="value" >}}` syntax

## Eureka Theme Specifics

### Widget System
- Homepage widgets: experience, about, pages, etc.
- Configure in `content/homepage/` with widget handlers
- Widget types defined in theme's `archetypes/`
- Each widget has specific frontmatter requirements

### Content Types
- Posts: Standard blog posts with tags/categories
- Docs: Hierarchical documentation with table of contents
- Authors: Author profiles with social links
- Homepage: Special pages for homepage sections

### Customization
- Override theme templates by copying to `layouts/`
- Modify styles via `assets/` or `static/`
- Configure via `params.yaml` and `config.yaml`
- Use partials for reusable components
- Never modify theme files directly (use Hugo Modules)

### Best Practices
- Always test locally before deploying
- Use draft mode for work-in-progress content
- Keep frontmatter consistent across content types
- Follow Eureka's content structure conventions
- Reference Eureka documentation for widget configuration
- Use `hugo mod` commands to update theme

## Git Workflow
- Main branch: `main`
- Auto-deployment: Pushes to main trigger GitHub Actions workflow
- Never commit `public/` directory (it's in .gitignore)
- Commit messages follow Angular commit convention (feat, fix, docs, etc.)

## Important Notes
- Base URL: https://zjingwang.github.io/
- The site uses Hugo Modules for theme management (requires Go 1.12+)
- Theme version: Eureka v0.9.3
- GitHub Actions automatically builds and deploys on push to main
- Local development: run `hugo server` and visit http://localhost:1313
- Hugo version: v0.111.0 (compatible with Eureka v0.9.3)
- If encountering POSTCSS errors, ensure Hugo version is 0.100.0 or higher
- Use `hugo mod clean` if experiencing module cache issues
- Use `/data/tools/hugo/hugo` if PATH has multiple Hugo versions

## Document Creation and Preview Workflow

### Default Workflow for New Documents
When creating new documents (posts, docs, or pages), follow this workflow:

1. **Create the document** using Hugo commands or manually:
   ```bash
   hugo new posts/article-name.md
   hugo new docs/topic/details/doc-name.md
   hugo new homepage/page-name.md
   ```

2. **Start preview server** (default action after creating documents):
   ```bash
   hugo server -D
   ```
   - Server runs on http://localhost:1313 by default
   - Use `hugo server -D` to include draft content
   - Use `/data/tools/hugo/hugo` if PATH has multiple Hugo versions

3. **Browse and test the new page** using Browser tools:
   - Navigate to the new page URL (e.g., http://localhost:1313/posts/article-name/)
   - Verify the page renders correctly
   - Check that all features work as expected:
     - Page title and metadata display correctly
     - Content formatting is proper
     - Navigation links work
     - Images and assets load correctly
     - Responsive layout works
     - Table of contents (if enabled) displays correctly
     - Tags and categories appear properly

4. **Verify functionality**:
   - Test page navigation (back/forward, menu links)
   - Check search functionality if applicable
   - Verify tags and categories display correctly
   - Ensure author information is shown properly
   - Test any interactive elements
   - Verify comment system works (if enabled)

### Browser Testing Guidelines
- Always use Browser tools to visually inspect new pages
- Test on the actual rendered page, not just the Markdown source
- Verify both desktop and mobile views if possible
- Check console for any JavaScript errors
- Ensure all links and navigation work correctly
- Verify images load and display properly
- Check that code blocks are highlighted correctly

### Preview Best Practices
- Preview should be the default step after creating any new content
- Don't skip preview even for simple documents
- Fix any issues found during preview before committing
- Document any known issues or limitations in comments
- Test with `draft: false` before final commit
- Verify frontmatter is correctly formatted

## Troubleshooting

### Common Issues
- **POSTCSS errors**: Upgrade Hugo to 0.100.0+ or use `hugo mod clean`
- **Module cache issues**: Run `hugo mod clean` and `hugo mod download`
- **Date parsing errors**: Ensure `lastmod` field uses valid ISO 8601 format
- **Template not found**: Check layout lookup order and file paths
- **Assets not loading**: Verify paths in `static/` or `assets/` directories
- **Build failures**: Check Hugo version compatibility with Eureka theme

### Debugging Tips
- Use `hugo server --verbose` for detailed build information
- Check `resources/_gen/` for processed assets
- Review browser console for JavaScript errors
- Validate YAML frontmatter syntax
- Test with minimal content to isolate issues
